# UI style

- Follow `docs/ui-style.md` for the game's palette, component states, art and layout rules.
- Use tokens in `apps/web/src/ui/theme.css` for CSS; add new tokens there rather than introducing one-off colours in a screen.
- Use `GameButton`, `IconButton`, `PanelHeading` and `EmptyState` from `apps/web/src/ui/primitives.tsx` for new panels and actions.
- Use `ART`, `INK` and `STROKE` from `apps/web/src/art/palette.ts` for new SVG art. Keep the 2 px dark-green outline and restrained fill palette.
- Keep characters in the existing scene coordinates and products in the 40×48 frame. Give every new upgrade its own `UpgradeArt` illustration.
- Preserve the fixed-step simulation and command path. UI reads state and dispatches commands; it does not change game rules.
- Make important controls at least 44 px tall, give keyboard focus a visible ring, and show status with text or shape as well as colour.
- Keep the main service tray available on portrait phones and the scene beside the tray on landscape tablets.
- For new products, add a distinct 40×48 `ProductArt`, a named request and a need request, and make the request reachable from an archetype. Keep the scene and tray on the same shared catalog page (5 products). Use `CatalogControls` in the inventory view.
- Collapse the service tray to operator status while an NPC runs the counter; show detailed selling controls only when the player runs it. Keep staff cards scannable and details collapsible.
- Keep every main screen and dialog within one 100dvh viewport including primary buttons and safe areas. If content grows, scroll the inner content while keeping the primary action visible; verify 320×568, 375×667, 390×844 and landscape tablet. Apply this to day summaries, return dialogs, onboarding and future overlays.
- Prioritize large bold outcome numbers in summaries, with green for positive and red for negative plus explicit labels. Collapse secondary metrics. Keep both counters visible on narrow screens, use 44px counter choices and explicit target counter when assigning staff. Keep shift and station controls collapsed until clicked; progress fills must reflect nonzero values.
- Never draw a red cross, green cross logo, real pharmacy brand, real drug or dosage. Read `docs/content-rules.md` before adding game content.
- Run `npm run check` and `npm run build` after UI changes.
